#!/usr/bin/env python3
# =============================================================================
#  tuisla — A Tesla TUI
#
#  USAGE:  python3 tuisla [--mode MODE] [--unit UNIT] [--refresh S] [--invert]
#                         [--simple] [--color]
#          python3 tuisla -l|--login            (both steps below)
#          python3 tuisla --login-tesla [--print]
#          python3 tuisla --login-mtm
#
#  LOGIN:  --login-tesla signs in to Tesla in the browser and saves a refresh
#          token to $XDG_STATE_HOME/tuisla/refresh_token (~/.local/state/...),
#          mode 600.  tuisla keeps that file up to date when Tesla rotates the
#          token.  --print writes the token to stdout instead of saving it.
#          --login-mtm opens the MyTeslaMate Fleet page and asks for the token
#          shown there (Enter skips), saved as .../tuisla/myteslamate_token.
#
#  MODES:  Vehicle data is always read from the Tesla Owner API; the mode only
#          decides where commands go.
#    ro    Read-only; commands are disabled.
#    mtm   (default) Commands go to MyTeslaMate (api.myteslamate.com) using the
#          MyTeslaMate token.  The Tesla token is not sent to them.
#    vc    Commands go to a local tesla-http-proxy (teslamotors/vehicle-command)
#          at VEHICLE_COMMAND_URL.  NOTE: the proxy expects a Fleet API token
#          from a registered Tesla developer app and a key paired with the car;
#          the Owner API token tuisla uses will most likely be rejected.
#
#  UNITS:  metric | us (temperatures typed in commands follow the unit)
#
#  ENV:
#    TESLA_REFRESH_TOKEN    Optional. Used instead of the saved token if set.
#                           Without any token tuisla runs in demo mode.
#    TESLA_VIN              Optional. Pin to a specific vehicle; by default the
#                           first vehicle on the account is used.
#    MYTESLAMATE_TOKEN      Optional. Used instead of the saved MyTeslaMate
#                           token if set; mtm needs one or the other.
#    VEHICLE_COMMAND_URL    Default: https://localhost:4443
#    VEHICLE_COMMAND_CERT   CA file for the proxy's TLS cert. Default: cert.pem
#                           (relative to the current directory)
# =============================================================================

